{"id":"e07t4","name":"Meter Display Reader","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["screen"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Old electricity meters show their value on a seven-segment display. A camera takes a picture of the display and turns it into text. You are given <code>screen</code>, a list of strings: every group of <b>3 lines</b> is one row of the display, and inside a row every group of <b>3 characters</b> is one digit, drawn with <code>_</code>, <code>|</code> and spaces:</p>\n<pre class=\"exv\"> _     _  _     _  _  _  _  _ \n| |  | _| _||_||_ |_   ||_||_|\n|_|  ||_  _|  | _||_|  ||_| _|</pre>\n<p>These are the digits <code>0</code> to <code>9</code>. All lines have the same length, which is a multiple of 3, and the number of lines is a multiple of 3.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one string per row of the display: the digits of the row, from left to right. A group of 3x3 characters that is not one of the ten digits is written <code>\"?\"</code>. If a row contains at least one <code>\"?\"</code>, add <code>\" ILL\"</code> at the end of its string.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>screen = [\" _     _  _     _  _  _  _  _ \", \"| |  | _| _||_||_ |_   ||_||_|\", \"|_|  ||_  _|  | _||_|  ||_| _|\"]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"0123456789\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.string screen<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(screen):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["grille 3x3","découper en blocs","dictionnaire de motifs","consigne longue"],"minutes":22,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"screen":[" _     _  _     _  _  _  _  _ ","| |  | _| _||_||_ |_   ||_||_|","|_|  ||_  _|  | _||_|  ||_| _|"]},"expected":{"value":["0123456789"]}},{"input":{"screen":["    _ ","|_| _|","  ||_ ","   _|_","|_| | ","  ||_ "]},"expected":{"value":["42","4? ILL"]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}